{"id": "EUVD-2026-98700", "enisaUuid": "3bbe4a40-bf79-328e-8c1f-44eb9f4226ed", "description": "FreeRDP 3.0.0-beta1 before 3.32.0, when built with verbose WinPR assertions and using smartcard emulation, has a reachable assertion: the emulated SCardStatusA passes a NULL reader-name destination to scard_copy_strings. A malicious RDP server can send an SCardStatusA request with fmszReaderNamesIsNULL=1 to abort a connecting client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:57:50", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-996j-34w6-5hgm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-beta1-before-3.32.0-reachable-assertion-via-emulated-scardstatusa"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9rqv-83g7-qj3p", "CVE-2026-109678"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d2c2d355-e131-31fd-8af2-521cd86e9f0d", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0-beta1 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0c038e01-6ee0-3bfc-9efb-c9e74745944d", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}